        {
          "type": "worked_example",
          "title": "Evaluating a mixed expression",
          "problem": "Evaluate -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6 - (-5).",
          "steps": [
            "Step 1: Do multiplication and division first, left to right. -3 x (-4) = 12. (-18) / 6 = -3.",
            "Step 2: Rewrite: 12 + (-3) - (-5).",
            "Step 3: Subtract negative = add positive: 12 + (-3) + 5.",
            "Step 4: Add left to right: 12 - 3 = 9, then 9 + 5 = 14."
          ],
          "answer": "14"
        },
        {
          "type": "common_mistake",
          "text": "Adding before dividing is wrong. In -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6, division goes before addition. Correct order gives 9."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "cta",
          "text": "Ready to practice. Continue to the regular exercise for 6 questions."
        }
      ],
      "source_text": "Lesson 3.1 - Order of operations\nSkill: S4\nObjective:\n1. Evaluate expressions using order of operations.\nOrder of operations\nWhen an expression has more than one operation:\n1. Grouping first: ( ), [ ], { }.\n2. Multiply and divide, left to right.\n3. Add and subtract, left to right.\nWorked example\nProblem: Evaluate -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6 - (-5).\nStep 1: Do multiplication and division first, left to right.\n-3 x (-4) = 12\n(-18) / 6 = -3\nStep 2: Rewrite: 12 + (-3) - (-5).\nStep 3: Subtract negative = add positive: 12 + (-3) + 5.\nStep 4: Add left to right: 12 - 3 = 9, then 9 + 5 = 14.\nAnswer: 14.\nCommon mistake\nAdding before dividing is wrong. In -3 x (-4) + (-18) / 6, division goes before addition. Correct order gives 9."
    }
  },
